# Scan flow version — ask before every change

Before implementing **any** code change in this project, ask the user which version to target:

- **26A** — previous scanner experience
- **26B** — Q2 2026 work in progress (default / shared components)
- **Both** — apply the same change to both versions

Use the **AskQuestion** tool when available. Do not start editing until the user answers.

## Exceptions (no need to ask)

- Purely informational questions (explain, review, debug without editing)
- Changes explicitly scoped by the user (e.g. "fix this in 26B only")
- Version-picker / version-manager plumbing only (`FlowVersionPickerPage`, `scanFlowVersionManager`)

## Where each version lives

| Version | Location | Pattern |
|---------|----------|---------|
| **26A** | `Scanner/src/components/26A/` | `*26A.tsx`, `*26A.ts` |
| **26B** | `Scanner/src/components/` (shared root) | No `26A` suffix |
| **Routing** | `Scanner/src/App.tsx` | Branches on `scanFlowVersion` |

## How to apply changes

- **26A only** → edit files under `components/26A/`; do not change shared 26B components unless needed for compile/routing.
- **26B only** → edit shared components at `components/` root; do not change `26A/` files.
- **Both** → mirror the change in the 26A-specific file **and** the equivalent shared (26B) file. If no 26A counterpart exists, say so and confirm with the user.

## Example

User: "Change the scan toolbar button color to blue."

Agent: Ask — **26A**, **26B**, or **both**? Then edit `ScanToolbar26A.tsx`, `ScanToolbar.tsx`, or both accordingly.
